    summary: 'Because the GIL bounds a Python process to one core of bytecode, parallelism at the application layer comes from processes: prefork HTTP workers, data-loader workers, and one engine process per GPU or one worker per tensor-parallel rank. Each process has its own interpreter, heap and CUDA context, so communication between them goes through pipes, sockets, shared memory or the GPU fabric rather than shared objects.',
