    summary: 'In eager mode every tensor operation in Python is executed immediately: the call goes through the Python binding, the dispatcher and a device kernel launch, then returns a tensor wrapper while the GPU runs asynchronously. Host overhead per op is of the order of microseconds (commonly several to tens, depending on the op and whether autograd is active), which is negligible for a large GEMM and dominant for a small elementwise op. A model is therefore fast in eager mode when its ops are big, and launch-bound when they are small or numerous.',
