    mechanics: 'A pybind11 module defines functions and classes; each call unpacks `PyObject*` arguments into C++ values (tensors are passed as `at::Tensor` handles, no copy), runs the body, and packs the return value. Releasing the GIL with `py::gil_scoped_release` or `Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS` around the native work is what allows other Python threads to run during a kernel launch sequence or an NCCL call; forgetting it makes the extension serialize the process. `torch.utils.cpp_extension` compiles C++/CUDA sources with `nvcc` against the installed PyTorch headers, either ahead of time (`setup.py`) or just-in-time (`load`, `load_inline`), and the resulting `.so` registers ops via `TORCH_LIBRARY` so they dispatch like built-ins and can be traced by torch.compile. The C++ ABI of the extension must match the PyTorch build (compiler, `_GLIBCXX_USE_CXX11_ABI`, PyTorch version) and its CUDA code must be compiled for the target compute capabilities (`TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST`), or the module fails to import or the kernel fails at launch. `ctypes` and `cffi` call plain C functions without a compile step and release the GIL by default, but cannot handle tensors without passing raw pointers and shapes manually. Binding overhead is of the order of a microsecond per call plus argument conversion; extensions that take many small Python objects pay proportionally.',
    input: 'Python calls with tensors and scalars; compiled shared objects loaded at import.',
    output: 'Native execution (CPU code or CUDA launches) and results wrapped back into Python objects.',
    compute: 'Binding overhead of roughly a microsecond per call; the native body runs at full speed and, when the GIL is released, in parallel with Python.',
    knobs: ['GIL release around native work', 'AOT vs JIT compilation of the extension', 'TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST and PTX inclusion for forward compatibility', 'C++ ABI flag matching the framework build', 'Registering ops via torch.library for dispatcher and compiler visibility', 'Static vs dynamic linking of CUDA libraries'],
